# Build context for the Dockerfile. Nothing secret and nothing machine-specific goes into an image.
# Secrets and local configuration, at ANY depth (a nested packages/app/.env.local must never enter `COPY packages`).
# CI plants such files in the checkout and asserts they are not in the image (job `image`, AC6).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/storybook-static
**/*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Repository and agent tooling, never needed to build or run the app
.git
.github
.claude
.agents
.ai
.mcp.json
skills-lock.json
agent

# Docs and local files
*.md
.DS_Store
*.log

# Image and Compose files do not belong inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
